      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can both file_offs and buf_offs be page unaligned while (file_offs !\u003d buf_offs)? I thought that\u0027s the case we can\u0027t handle without moving the data after read because either file offset we read or buffer offset we write will have to be page-unaligned.\n\nAlso I think there is a case when start_bounce_len would be more than PAGE_SIZE. Say buf_offs\u003d3K and file_offs\u003d1K, then direct_read_start_offs \u003d PAGE_ALIGN(3K + 4K - 1K) \u003d 8K, so direct_read_start_offs is 5K ahead of buf_offs, which is more than one page.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 175,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 175,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
